 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Nine in ten Israeli trips abroad leave by plane.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Because Israel's borders aren't exactly road-trip friendly.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "North: Lebanon and Syria. Closed.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "South and east: Egypt and Jordan. Open, since the peace treaties of 1979 and 1994.",
   "screen": "Peace: Egypt *1979,* Jordan *1994*",
   "at": "L3:open",
   "gap": 0.12,
   "until": "L4",
   "screen_size": 60
  },
  {
   "say": "Still, almost everyone takes off from here.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "So who travels abroad the most? Trips per person, in 2019.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Israel: about one trip a year. Twice the Americans.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Brits and Germans travel more. But six in ten German trips abroad go by car, bus or train.",
   "screen": "Germany: *6 in 10* trips abroad by land",
   "at": "L7:six",
   "gap": 0.12,
   "until": "L8"
  },
  {
   "say": "Count only flights, and Israelis fly abroad almost twice as often as Germans.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Over a lifetime, that's roughly eighty trips abroad.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "And since 2020, the Abraham Accords added direct flights to Dubai and Abu Dhabi.",
   "screen": "Since *2020:* direct flights to the UAE",
   "at": "L10:since",
   "gap": 0.12,
   "until": "L11"
  },
  {
   "say": "If the neighbours ever open up, we'll drive. Where would you go first?",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "If you love Israeli facts, follow Noam Roz for more.",
   "wav": "ref/follow_line_noam.wav",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Until then, nine in ten of us leave by plane.",
   "gap": 0.1
  }
 ],
