 },
 "caption_en": "Most countries can drive out. Israelis mostly can't. ✈️\n\n🛫 9 in 10 trips abroad by Israelis leave by plane: 88.7% by air, 9.7% by land, 1.6% by sea (CBS, 2023).\n\nThe neighbours: Lebanon and Syria, closed. Egypt (peace treaty 1979) and Jordan (1994), open at Taba, Allenby and other crossings.\n\nTrips abroad per person, 2019 (World Bank departures / population): UAE 2.0, UK 1.4, Germany 1.2, Israel 1.0, Saudi Arabia 0.9, France 0.7, USA 0.5, Jordan 0.14, Türkiye 0.12, Egypt no data. Israelis travel abroad about twice as often as Americans.\n\nGermans and Brits travel more, but 6 in 10 German trips abroad go by land (Eurostat, 2023).\n\nTrips abroad by plane per person, 2023: Israel 0.81 (CBS departures x air share), Netherlands 0.52, Germany 0.46, EU 0.33, France 0.27, Spain 0.22, Italy 0.11 (Eurostat trips of 1+ nights). Different definitions, so read it as a rough comparison.\n\nOver a lifetime of 80+ years, about one trip a year adds up to roughly 80 trips abroad (rough estimate).\n\nSince 2020, the Abraham Accords added direct flights to the UAE. If the neighbours ever open up, we'll drive. Where would you go first?\n\nSources: CBS Statistical Abstract of Israel 2024; World Bank ST.INT.DPRT and SP.POP.TOTL; Eurostat tour_dem_tttr.\nPhotos (Wikimedia Commons): Ben Gurion Airport, Rakoon (CC0); Allenby Bridge, Kounosu (CC BY-SA 3.0); Austria-Germany border, High Contrast (CC BY 3.0 de); El Al 787, km30192002 (CC BY 2.0).",
 "caption_he": "9 מכל 10 נסיעות של ישראלים לחו\"ל יוצאות בטיסה (למ\"ס, 2023).\nבממוצע ישראלי נוסע לחו\"ל בערך פעם בשנה, פי 2 מאמריקאי. גרמנים ובריטים נוסעים יותר, אבל 6 מכל 10 נסיעות של גרמנים לחו\"ל הן ביבשה.\nבטיסות בלבד, ישראלים טסים לחו\"ל כמעט פי 2 מגרמנים.\nאם השכנים ייפתחו יום אחד, ניסע באוטו. לאן הייתם נוסעים קודם?"
}